    {
      "itemId": "86416c75-203b-43f2-ad66-27b13eb2a20c",
      "text": "Start with 31 apples.\n\n5×12 = 60 and 4×4 = 16, so 31 + 60 + 16 = 107.\nDoubling twice: 107×2×2 = 428.\nNo damaged apples are removed. Splitting equally into 4 rooms gives 428÷4 = 107 apples per room. Keeping one room leaves **107** apples.\n\n107",
      "toolCalls": 1,
      "error": null
    },
    {
      "itemId": "85d26873-30e1-4dca-bd46-64cb6c835e13",
      "text": "87",
